:"offering","H5560":"fine flour","H1101":"to mix","H8081":"oil","H7969":"three","H6241":"tenth","H8147":"two","H8163":"hairy","H5795":"goat","H2403":"sin","H3722":"to atone","H5921":"upon","H905":"pole","H8548":"continually","H5262":"drink offering","H4941":"judgement","H801":"food offering","H6218":"ten","H2088":"this","H6031":"be occupied","H853":"[Obj.]","H5315":"soul","H7126":"come","H3725":"atonement","H2568":"five","H6240":"ten","H2287":"to celebrate","H2282":"feast","H702":"four","H8145":"second","H4557":"number","H7992":"third","H6249":"eleven","H7243":"fourth","H6235":"ten","H2549":"fifth","H8672":"nine","H8345":"sixth","H8083":"eight","H8066":"eighth","H6116":"assembly","H428":"these","H4150":"time appointed","H5088":"vow","H5071":"voluntariness","H8002":"peace offering","H559":"to say","H4872":"Moses","H413":"to(wards)","H3478":"Israel","H834":"which","H6680":"to command"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["haydock",1,null,"haydock","The first. This day was doubly solemn, as being the first day of the month, consequently entitled to all the sacrifices enjoined for it; and also a holiday, for which other victims are requisite, besides the perpetual holocausts, ver. 2, 6., and chap. xxviii. 11. (Haydock)"],["haydock",7,null,"haydock","Tenth. The feast of expiation, on which see Leviticus xvi. 29., and xxiii. 24, where we have also explained what relates to the feast of tabernacles, ver. 34."],["haydock",12,null,"haydock","Seven days, not refraining indeed all that time from servile work, but remaining under tents, and daily performing what is required, ver. 13., &c."],["haydock",35,null,"haydock","Eighth day, which was more solemn than the preceding ones, but less so than the first. The victims are every day diminished. (Calmet) — This day, in the Hebrew calendar, is called the feast of retention, (atsroth) as they staid near the tabernacle. (Du Hamel)"],["haydock",39,null,"haydock","Vows. The general regulations did not hinder any private ones from being fulfilled. (Calmet) — Sacrifice. Mincha, or offering of flour, &c. (Haydock)"]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]}}